To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$, $\blueD{\text{ multiply it by }\dfrac{1}{4}}$ and then $\goldE{\text{add } 1} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{4}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{y} &= \greenD{4}\blueD{\times \dfrac{1}{4}}\goldE{+1} \\\\
\maroonD{y} &= \maroonD{2}
\end{align}$
